# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# This directory IS the public repository: github.com/carnworkstudios/docforensics
#
# It is an allowlist, not an ignore list, and the difference is the whole
# point. An ignore list fails open: the first time you drop a directory of
# checkpoints or a scratch notebook in here, a list of things-to-exclude has
# never heard of it and publishes it. Denying everything and naming what ships
# fails closed instead — a new file is invisible until somebody adds a line.
#

# ── Then name what ships ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes
!/README.md
!/LICENSE.md
!/CITATION.cff
!/docs/
!/examples/
!/npm/
!/python/

# ── The push scripts stay local ────────────────────────────────────────────
# They are the operator's tooling, not the product. The deny-all above already
# excludes the root one; this catches the copies inside re-included
# directories, where the allowlist has stopped protecting anything.
**/push.sh

# ── Weights are not in git ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# They live in ../huggingface/, so there is one file in the world with one
# hash, which is what makes the compliance fingerprint mean anything.
*.onnx
*.onnx.data
*.ort
*.pt
*.pth
weights/

# ── Build output and local noise ───────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
dist/
build/
*.tgz
*.whl
*.egg-info/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
.env
.env.*
*.log

# ── Never, under any circumstances ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Listed even though the deny-all above already covers them, because a future
# edit that re-includes a directory should still hit a wall here.
**/token
**/*.pem
**/*.key
.hf_token
.npmrc
.pypirc
